---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="A little more about Ernest Au — background, what I work on, and what I'm figuring out."
>
  <div class="page">
    <section class="head">
      <p class="label">about</p>
      <h1>A bit more context</h1>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Placeholder copy — replace this with your own. A good about page usually
        answers three questions in order: what you do now, how you got here, and
        what you're currently curious about.
      </p>
      <p>
        The second paragraph is a good place for specifics. Which languages and
        systems you actually reach for, the kind of problems you like, and any
        work you're proud of. Concrete beats impressive: naming the thing you
        built and what broke tells a reader far more than a list of adjectives.
      </p>
      <p>
        Close with what you're figuring out right now, and how to reach you.
        People who land here and want to talk should not have to hunt for it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 4.5rem) 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .head .label { margin-block-end: 1.25rem; }

  .prose {
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
